            %li#Perrone24
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Perrone"}> Paolo Perrone
                , Chapter 6 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Starting Category Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/13670"} doi:10.1142/13670
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1912.10642"} arXiv:1912.10642
          %p
            Exposition of basics of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+algebra"} categorical algebra
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes"} geometry of physics – categories and toposes
              , Section 2:
              %em
                %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#BasicNotionsOfCategoricalAlgebra"} Basic notions of categorical algebra
          %p
            A survey of definitions of symmetric monoidal categories,
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+functor"} symmetric monoidal functor
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+natural+transformation"} symmetric monoidal natural transformation
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/qg-fall2004/definitions.pdf"} Some definitions everyone should know
          %p For an elementary introduction to symmetric monoidal categories using string diagrams, see:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"} John Baez
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Stay"} Mike Stay
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/rosetta.pdf"} Physics, topology, logic and computation: a Rosetta Stone
          %p The theorem that symmetric monoidal categories model all connective spectra is due to
          %ul#Thomason
            %li
              R. Thomason,
              %em Symmetric monoidal categories model all connective spectra
              , Theory and applications of Categories, Vol. 1, No. 5, (1995) pp. 78-118
          %p More discussion is in
          %ul#Mandell
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"}> Michael Mandell
              ,
              %em An Inverse K-Theory Functor
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.3622"}> arXiv:1002.3622
              )
          %ul#Sharma
            %li#FongSpivak
              %p
